---
const principles = [
  {
    q: 'What would reduce barriers to access?',
    body: 'Reach is usually capped by something other than interest. At one high school it was teacher confidence, not student appetite. Find the real cap first.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How do I meet this person where they are, emotionally, physically, and mindfully?',
    body: 'Physically counts. K-2 students tapping haphazardly on tablets was a dexterity problem that looked like an engagement problem until we watched them.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How does their stage of life change how they learn?',
    body: 'A six year old and a ten year old are not the same user, and neither are a first year teacher and a twenty year veteran. Design for the band, not the average.',
  },
];

const process = [
  {
    step: 'Discover',
    body: 'Ask the right questions, then test whether they are the right questions. Read the research, read the market, pay attention to what is happening outside the building.',
  },
  {
    step: 'Define',
    body: 'Decide what success means and be rigorous about it before anything gets built. A metric chosen after launch is a metric chosen to look good.',
  },
  {
    step: 'Scope',
    body: 'Don\'t try to solve the world. Pick a few problems, solve them properly, and build from there. Breadth is how good products become mediocre ones.',
  },
  {
    step: 'Prototype',
    body: 'With product, engineering, and curriculum in the room. Adobe through Cursor and Claude, shipped to a sandbox or Vercel, against an AI-friendly design system. The prototype linked in my Experience case study was built this way, and so were the products in the section below.',
  },
  {
    step: 'Test where the work happens',
    body: 'A teacher in her own classroom, fielding three other students mid-task, tells you more than a recruited participant behind glass who set aside a clean hour. Both are useful. The second is rare and worth arranging.',
  },
];
---

<section class="how" data-reveal>
  <div class="section-label">how I work</div>

  <div class="how-intro">
    <h2>Three questions, whatever I'm building</h2>
    <p>
      These are the questions I bring to a problem before I have any idea what the answer looks
      like. They hold whether the person on the other side is eight years old, teaching third
      period, or sitting in a waiting room.
    </p>
  </div>

  <ol class="principles">
    {principles.map(({ q, body }) => (
      <li class="principle">
        <h3>{q}</h3>
        <p>{body}</p>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>

  <div class="how-process">
    <div class="process-head">
      <h2>And a process I actually follow</h2>
      <p>
        I know a product has to be paid for. I've worked on the flagship that keeps the lights on,
        and I've learned that influence, storytelling, and clear communication are what let a design
        decision survive contact with a business. Values that can't be shipped aren't worth much.
      </p>
    </div>

    <dl class="steps">
      {process.map(({ step, body }) => (
        <div class="step">
          <dt>{step}</dt>
          <dd>{body}</dd>
        </div>
      ))}
    </dl>

    <p class="how-note">
      One thing that has genuinely changed: the handoff got short. Work that used to live in Figma
      now often goes straight into code against a design system, so there is far less to translate
      and considerably more time for edge cases and polish. That part is a real improvement.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .how {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 72px 48px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 44px;
  }

  .how-intro,
  .process-head {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 16px;
    max-width: 620px;
  }

  .how h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: clamp(26px, 3.2vw, 36px);
    font-weight: 300;
    line-height: 1.15;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .how-intro p,
  .process-head p {
    font-size: 16px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
  }

  /* ---- principles ---- */
  .principles {
    list-style: none;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(250px, 1fr));
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--ink-faint);
    border: 0.5px solid var(--ink-faint);
    counter-reset: principle;
  }

  .principle {
    background: var(--warm-white);
    padding: 28px 24px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 12px;
    counter-increment: principle;
  }

  .principle h3 {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 21px;
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.25;
    color: var(--ink);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .principle h3::before {
    content: counter(principle, decimal-leading-zero);
    display: block;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.22em;
    color: var(--teal);
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }

  .principle p {
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
  }

  /* ---- process ---- */
  .how-process {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 32px;
    padding-top: 24px;
    border-top: 0.5px solid var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .steps {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 0;
  }

  .step {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 210px minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: 32px;
    padding: 18px 0;
    border-top: 0.5px solid var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .step:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0.5px solid var(--ink-faint);
  }

  .step dt {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 20px;
    color: var(--ink);
    line-height: 1.25;
  }

  .step dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    max-width: 60ch;
  }

  .how-note {
    font-size: 14.5px;
    line-height: 1.75;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    max-width: 66ch;
  }

  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .how { padding: 56px 24px; gap: 34px; }
    .step { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 6px; }
  }
</style>
